with over 20 million followers Donald  Trump is the 68th most followed person  on Twitter twitter has been by far  Trump's most frequent mode of  communication to the public throughout  the 2016 primaries the general election  and as president elect Trump once  tweeted many people have said I'm the  world's greatest writer of 140 character  sentences Trump has obviously been an  unorthodox political candidate and  president-elect in the way that he  speaks and conducts himself in person  like in debates and at rallies and we've  seen him carry that over to his tweeting  taking the conventions of how  politicians use social media and  throwing them out the window  his impulsive bold bombastic demeanor  has translated verbatim to his use of  Twitter where he regularly touts his  accomplishments hastily mocks people and  doesn't always check facts Trump is said  when he becomes president that he'll  dial back the tone of his tweets and  it'll be fascinating to see whether or  not he keeps this promise as undoubtedly  we've never seen a u.s. president carry  himself the way that Donald Trump does  on Twitter it would probably be  destructive or at the very least  extremely odd to have a US president  that is constantly sending out little  daily messages on the Internet bragging  about how great he is or insulting  anyone who crosses him thus far right up  to his inauguration Trump has proven  that he has absolutely no ability to  withstand criticism and just brush  anything off even little things like  when an actor criticizes him this is the  definition of being thin-skinned he has  shown us time and again for years now  that he must unconditionally pick up his  phone and ridicule almost anyone that  says something negative about him this  is not a great trait for a president we  will have to wait and see how his  Twitter use evolves as president if it  does but I thought it would be  interesting to take a look back at  Donald Trump's history on Twitter prior  to becoming president since the  beginning of the 2016 election cycle  Trump has averaged about 11 tweets a day  and the longest he's gone without  tweeting was only for a day and a half  this past November he once tweeted 87  times in one day  his personal record on October 19th of  2016 sometimes it's just a way for him  to check in with the public and send a  little greeting like last May when he  wished everyone a happy Cinco de Mayo  and said the best taco bowls are made in  Trump Tower Grill I love Hispanics  sometimes it's a way for him to channel  his thoughts about issues that are  important to him like the 117 tweets he  has posted saying that climate change is  a hoax or is unimportant including a  total of 47 tweets saying that global  warming isn't real because it was cold  at the moment he was tweeting or his 31  tweets implying that vaccinations cause  autism or his 84 tweets suggesting that  President Obama was born in Kenya and  sometimes Trump uses Twitter as an  outlet for his signature brand of  no-holds-barred confrontational  communication that brash politically  incorrect delivery that so many of the  trumpet supporters love like the 61  times he tweeted about Rosie O'Donnell  or his hundred and fifty-eight tweets  about megyn kelly or either of these  classic tweets Mitt Romney had his  chance to beat a failed president but he  choked like a dog now he calls me racist  but I am the least racist person there  is and sorry losers and haters but my IQ  is one of the highest and you all know  it please don't feel so stupid or  insecure it's not your fault it's mostly  easy to tell which tweets are written by  Trump and which ones are written by  people who work for him data scientist  David Robinson analyzed the text from  Trump's Twitter account and found that  tweets containing messages that are  angry hyperbolic or braggadocious tweets  that use exclamation points and  emotionally charged words like crazy or  dumb tend to come from an Android mobile  operating system while the more benign  tweets things like links and photos or  positive messages come from an iPhone  it's known that Trump carries a samsung  galaxy which is an Android smartphone so  we can pretty firmly conclude  from the operating system and the  language that's used that generally  speaking tweets that say things like  Merry Christmas or thanks for coming out  to the rally today come from his social  media staff people like Brad parse kale  or dance Covino while Trump himself is  the author of tweets that convey things  like bragging and disdain Twitter also  seems to be one of Donald Trump's  favorite ways of negotiating financially  with private companies on December 6  Trump sent out a tweet about the  aircraft manufacturer Boeing saying that  their design for the new Air Force One  is too expensive Trump said Boeing is  building a brand-new 747 Air Force One  for future presidents but costs are out  of control more than four billion cancel  order even though both Boeing and the  White House said that Trump's claim  wasn't accurate Boeing stock price  quickly dropped after that tweet  a week later Trump took a shot at  defense contractor Lockheed Martin on  Twitter saying that they were charging  too much for f-35s after that tweet  Lockheed's market value dropped by four  billion dollars there is now actually a  mobile app that's been created that will  alert users when Donald Trump bad-mouths  a company so that they can sell while  the stock prices are down the developer  of the app said in a blog post this  one-of-a-kind trigger notifies you when  president-elect Trump tweets about a  publicly traded stock that you own in  real time these triggers can help you  capture moves or manage your holdings  based on the market's reaction to the  future president's remarks  the New York Times determined that about  one in every nine of trumps tweets is  some kind of insult on Twitter Trump has  used the word overrated thirty nine  times he's called someone a [ __ ] 52  times he said 55 times that someone  quote doesn't have a clue he's used the  phrase haters and losers 64 times he's  called someone a lightweight a hundred  and one times he's called someone stupid  one hundred and eighty three times he's  called someone dumb two hundred and  twenty-two times and on Twitter  is used the word loser 234 times he's  also ended 81 tweets with the word sad  followed by an exclamation point before  Ted Cruz dropped out of the Republican  primary  an analysis of Trump's tweets shows that  his twitter insults were abundantly  aimed at Republicans like when he  tweeted these two photos side-by-side  comparing his wife to Ted Cruz's wife  with the caption a picture is worth a  thousand words and during the general  election statistics show that his  twitter insults were mostly at Democrats  crooked Hillary crazy Bernie goofy  Elizabeth Warren and when Trump won the  presidency his insults towards  politicians saw a big drop-off but the  rate at which Trump insults the media on  Twitter has remained pretty constant  from rarely misses an opportunity to try  and discredit anyone in journalism who  says something unfavorable about him  whenever a news outlet runs a negative  story on him he's often quick to pull  out his phone and tweet about how stupid  or untrustworthy or unsuccessful the  news organization is according to Donald  Trump's tweets CNN is bad television  garbage and just plain dumb and most  recently fake news from his press  conference Fox News is totally biased  and disgusting MSNBC has no ratings the  BBC has zero credibility Univision might  be controlled by the Mexican government  the New York Times is poorly run and  manage the Wall Street Journal or a  bunch of dummies USA Today is a boring  newspaper with no mojo the New York  Daily News is a worthless dying loser  newspaper The Weekly Standard is failing  the New Hampshire union-leader is  failing the Des Moines Register is  seriously failing the National Review is  failing and dying and has been losing  for years New York magazine is a piece  of garbage Esquire magazine is boring  Vanity Fair is really really boring and  Time magazine quote looks really flimsy  Trump doesn't spare individuals in the  media either when they say something  negative  if you're a journalist online or on TV  questioning something that Donald Trump  has said or done there's a pretty good  chance that he'll hop on Twitter and get  his revenge against you Trump once  tweeted when someone attacks me I always  attack back except 100 times more this  has nothing to do with a tirade but  rather a way of life  according to Trump Katie Couric is a  third-rate reporter Arianna Huffington  is ugly both inside and out Barry Diller  is a sad and pathetic figure Touraine  the BLET is a truly stupid guy megyn  kelly is so average in every way George  Will is perhaps the most boring  political pundit on TV Frank Luntz is a  total loser Sherri Jacobus is a major  loser and really dumb Charles  Krauthammer is a boring dopey overrated  dummy clown John Oliver is very boring  Jon Stewart is overrated not smart and  has no talent Anna Navarro has no talent  bryant gumbel is an arrogant dumb racist  dope with no talent mika brzezinski is a  neurotic mess Chuck Todd is a real loser  with sleepy eyes that will be fired like  a dog Harry Hurt is a dummy dope Don  Lemon is a lightweight and dumb as a  rock Chris Matthews has the lowest IQ on  television and Erik Erikson is a major  sleaze buffoon total lowlife dummy Trump  once tweeted how come every time I show  anger disgust or impatience enemies say  I had a tantrum or meltdown stupid or  dishonest people shortly after winning  the election Trump claimed that he would  have won the popular vote if it weren't  for millions of illegal voters casting  ballots for Hillary Clinton of course  there's no evidence whatsoever to back  that up and when CNN senior Washington  correspondent Jeff Zeleny pointed that  out Trump attacked Zelan II by  retweeting a high-schooler Trump quoted  16-year old Seth Morton from California  who said pathetic  you have no sufficient evidence that  Donald Trump did not suffer from voter  fraud shame bad reporter  obviously pointing out that there's no  evidence that it didn't happen isn't  proof that it did happen common logical  fallacy but that aside you could tell  that this teenagers tweet wasn't  originally written by Trump because no  one was being called ugly or dumb  someone once sent a tweet to our new  president and said why do you always  insist on calling people names and  trying to taunt like a kid in a  schoolyard Trump replied only stupid  people when a president says something  people listen people act what the  president says matters and has national  and global impacts if Congress is voting  down a bill he likes is he going to go  on Twitter and start calling senators  losers if we're having a dispute with  another country is he going to tweet  that their president is a lightweight  [ __ ] this will be an embarrassment to  the United States Trump has said that  he'll be more presidential on social  media after he's sworn into office but  just a few days before his inauguration  he was on Twitter calling actress Meryl  Streep an overrated flunky because she  said something about him without even  mentioning him by name at the Golden  Globe Awards just close your eyes and  try to imagine Barack Obama or George W  Bush being so thin-skinned and reacting  that way try to picture one of those two  presidents or any other president for  that matter going on an angry  name-calling tirade just because some  celebrity said something about them it's  difficult to imagine this is the guy we  have representing the United States to  the rest of the world in charge of the  military responsible for diplomacy with  nations like Iran China North Korea when  it comes to Trump's promise to tighten  up on Twitter let's hope he does  differently than he's previewed during  his transition period and actually keeps  his word

